      {
        "id": "p15-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Use substitution to show that $y=x+b$ and $y=2x^2-7x+4$ intersect when\n$$2x^2-8x+(4-b)=0.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2x^2-8x+(4-b)=0$.",
          "worked": "Substituting $y=x+b$ into the parabola gives\n$$\\begin{align*}x+b&=2x^2-7x+4\\\\0&=2x^2-8x+4-b\\\\2x^2-8x+(4-b)&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Solve $\\Delta=0$ to find the value of $b$ for which the line is a tangent to the curve.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$b=-4$.\n\nTangency requires a repeated intersection root, so $\\Delta=0$.",
          "worked": "For $2x^2-8x+(4-b)=0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Delta&=(-8)^2-4\\times2(4-b)\\\\\\Delta&=32+8b.\\end{align*}$$\nThe line is tangent when there is one repeated intersection root, so\n$$\\begin{align*}32+8b&=0\\\\8b&=-32\\\\b&=-4.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
